  "description": "UMELOP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H140 Ce4 Co4 O53 P12 V4,0.33(C6 H14),0.67(C6 H12),0.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; V1 (V) has 5 O neighbors; V2 (V) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 0 O neighbors; V1A (V) has 5 O neighbors; V2A (V) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.929-4.810 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.69-147.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C68H140Ce4Co4O53P12V4·0.33(C6H14)·0.67(C6H12)·0.5(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 12 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
